-The practical lesson is to report component accounts alongside the aggregate. Returning to the orchard metaphor, a ledger of annual harvest alone cannot tell whether the trees, roots, and soil that support future harvests have changed. That physical record requires independent, comparable observations; it cannot be inferred from the account total. A harvest total is not a census of the orchard.
+Component accounts and independent physical observations provide complementary information and should be reported alongside the aggregate. Returning to the orchard metaphor, a ledger of annual harvest alone cannot tell whether the trees, roots, and soil that support future harvests have changed. That physical record requires independent, comparable observations; it cannot be inferred from the account total. A harvest total is not a census of the orchard.
 
